 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Precision:** The method relies on the accuracy of the depth estimation module (ENeRF cost volume). Inaccurate depth estimates may lead to suboptimal sampling probabilities [S1].
-*   **Boundaries:** The method specifically targets regions with "significant" variation. Flat regions with no variation receive fewer rays, which is intended to reduce redundancy but requires careful handling to ensure global scene coherence is maintained through the remaining samples [S1].
-*   **Degenerate Input:** If the depth estimation fails or the cost volume is ambiguous, the depth-guided component may provide misleading probabilities [S1].
